  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Prestidigitation is an old spell, dating back several editions. It has been a fixture of the Wizard’s arsenal for decades, and while its precise capabilities have changed in every edition, it has remained a powerful source of magic miscellany."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In 5th edition, Wizards of the Coast introduced similar spells (Druidcraft and Thaumaturgy) which fill a similar function but are tailored to the classes that use them, granting a similar magical utility option to every full spellcaster class."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In this article we’ll explore Prestidigitation and similar spells, exploring exactly what they can and can’t do, and weighing the merits of each spell against the others."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
